fore the provider request, under the existing code-owned executor-loss rule\",\"- **WHEN** historical tool activity mentions the removed `knowledge_read` id\\n- **THEN** a fresh attempt does not reconstruct or execute it from that history\");\nknowledge=knowledge.replace(\"- **WHEN** a Run accepted before removal has `knowledge_read` in its in-memory tool catalog\\n- **THEN** the Run fails closed before the provider request, under the existing code-owned executor-loss rule\",\"- **WHEN** historical tool activity mentions the removed `knowledge_read` id\\n- **THEN** a fresh attempt does not reconstruct or execute it from that history\");\nlet reader=req(\"tool-calling\",\"Conversation read uses the existing immutable read-only tool loop\");\nreader=reader.replace(\"immutable Run snapshot, execution rebinding\",\"attempt-local runtime catalog, trusted executor binding\").replaceAll(\"newly accepted Run\",\"newly prepared execution attempt\").replace(\"that Run snapshots its exact declaration\",\"that attempt retains its exact declaration in memory\");\nreader=reader.replace(\"Adding or changing the code-owned declaration or Chat-local sequence semantics SHALL use a coordinated API/worker/data cutover:\",\"Changing executable or Chat-local sequence semantics SHALL use a coordinated API/worker/data cutover; restart-applied description wording does not require a persisted declaration hash:\");\nlet availability=req(\"tool-calling\",\"Runtime tool availability is disclosed before the affected user turn\");\navailability=edit(availability,\"The API SHALL derive availability disclosure from strict server-authored semantic metadata, render the complete canonical context-item text before the triggering user message commits, and persist both together under producer `tool-availability`.\",\"The worker SHALL derive availability disclosure from its current attempt's admitted runtime state and the previous successful committed turn's minimal id/state record. It SHALL prepare canonical `tool-availability` context text for this attempt's model request and publish that text into message history only with successful turn completion.\");\navailability=availability.replace(\"current immutable manifest and the preceding accepted Run manifest\",\"current attempt's runtime state and the preceding successful turn's minimal id/state record\");\navailability=availability.replace(\"current Run SHALL bind and advertise the new declaration and declaration hash\",\"current attempt SHALL advertise its fresh in-memory declaration\");\navailability=edit(availability,\"A prior Run whose user-message/Run/snapshot transaction committed SHALL establish the prior availability baseline regardless of whether that Run later completed, failed, was cancelled, or expired. Its persisted availability block SHALL remain model-visible verbatim on later Runs until superseded by compaction or another context rewrite. A request that fails before the transaction commits SHALL establish no baseline.\",\"Only a successfully committed turn SHALL establish the comparison baseline. Its published reminder text remains model-visible until a context rewrite removes it. A failed, cancelled, expired, or superseded attempt SHALL publish no availability reminder to model history and SHALL not advance the baseline. Every retry compares with the same preceding committed turn, including after worker handoff.\");\navailability=edit(availability,\"When the most recent prior Run manifest is the legacy/unobserved sentinel, the current turn SHALL follow the same initial-baseline semantics: disclose currently eligible unavailable tools, do not emit Added entries for healthy tools, and persist an observed v1 manifest for the new Run.\",\"When there is no successful observed baseline, including migrated non-observation, the attempt SHALL use initial-baseline semantics. Successful completion SHALL store only its sorted exact ids and available/unavailable states; empty observed state is distinct from no observation.\");\navailability=availability.replace(\"first accepted turn\",\"first successfully committed turn\").replace(\"pre-compaction manifest\",\"pre-compaction record\").replace(\"immutable Run manifests\",\"attempt-local bindings\").replace(\"bound Run id\",\"Run/attempt id\");\navailability=availability.replace(\"latest prior Run uses the legacy/unobserved sentinel\",\"prior successful turn has no observed availability record\").replace(\"the new Run binds an observed v1 manifest\",\"successful completion stores the minimal observed id/state record\");\navailability=availability.replace(\"current manifest differs observably from the previous turn's manifest\",\"current attempt differs observably from the previous successful turn's id/state record\").replace(\"current Run advertises and binds the new native declaration and declaration hash\",\"current attempt advertises its new in-memory declaration without persisting it\");\navailability=availability.replace(\"#### Scenario: Failed prior Run still establishes the baseline\",\"#### Scenario: Failed prior attempt does not establish the baseline\");\navailability=edit(availability,\"- **WHEN** an accepted prior Run binds an availability manifest and later fails\\n- **THEN** the next turn compares against that prior Run's manifest\\n- **AND** its persisted availability text remains in portable history unchanged until a context rewrite removes it\",\"- **WHEN** an attempt prepares an availability transition but fails\\n- **THEN** a retry or later turn compares against the preceding successful committed turn\\n- **AND** the failed attempt's reminder does not enter model history\");\navailability=availability.replace(\"two turn snapshots with the same final availability and declaration\",\"two successful turn observations with the same availability\");\navailability += \"\\n\\n#### Scenario: Failed attempt observes a temporary outage\\n\\n- **WHEN** the previous committed message had grep available, an attempt sees it unavailable and fails, and its retry sees it available again\\n- **THEN** the retry emits no restoration notice because it compares with the previous committed message\\n- **AND** the failed attempt changes neither the comparison record nor model history\\n\\n#### Scenario: Baseline publication is atomic and fenced\\n\\n- **WHEN** a winning attempt successfully commits its assistant turn\\n- **THEN** its exact reminder text and minimal id/state record commit atomically with that completion\\n- **AND** stale or failed attempts cannot publish competing records\\n\";\nconst newState=`## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Availability comparison retains only committed tool identities and states\n\nA successfully committed turn SHALL retain an owner/chat-scoped comparison\nrecord consisting only of sorted exact tool ids and each id's \\`available\\` or\n\\`unavailable\\` state, associated with that turn's message/Run. It SHALL contain\nno schema, template, description, declaration/source hash, connection data, or\nraw failure detail. This record SHALL NOT be used for tool admission, execution,\nor reconstructing historical tool definitions.\n\nEvery attempt SHALL read the preceding successfully committed turn's record\nwithin its disclosure epoch. No observation SHALL remain distinct from an\nobserved empty record. Failed attempts and failed/cancelled/expired Runs SHALL\nnot establish or replace that baseline. The runtime catalog and safe current\nreasons SHALL remain in memory; only actual successfully published reminder\ntext may retain its rendered explanation.\n\n#### Scenario: Worker handoff preserves comparisons\n\n- **WHEN** a retry starts in another worker process\n- **THEN** it compares its fresh runtime state with the same persisted successful-turn id/state record\n- **AND** it does not need the previous worker's catalog or an in-memory cross-Run cache\n\n#### Scenario: Existing state is unobserved\n\n- **WHEN** no successful historical observation exists\n- **THEN** the attempt follows initial availability disclosure semantics\n- **AND** it does not treat missing observation as an empty historical catalog\n\n#### Scenario: Historical tool catalog storage is removed\n\n- **WHEN** the coordinated migration removes combined context snapshots\n- **THEN** only actual successful-turn id/state observations are retained for comparison\n- **AND** schemas, descriptions, declaration hashes, and raw manifest payloads are not retained through renamed fields\n`;\nconst removed=`## REMOVED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Tool availability is source-neutral and bound per Run\n\n**Reason**: Catalogs resolve in memory per execution attempt. Only minimal\nsuccessful-turn id/state observations persist for subsequent comparisons.\n\n**Migration**: Replace persisted versioned declaration-bearing manifests with\nthe minimal comparison record. Preserve successful observed empty states,\ntreat historical unobserved or failed Runs as having no baseline, and remove\ndeclaration hashes and full manifests without reconstructing historical tools.\n`;\nawait writeDraft(\"specs/tool-calling/spec.md\",\"## MODIFIED Requirements\\n\\n\"+[gate,failure,schema,observations,retry,knowledge,reader,availability].join(\"\\n\\n\")+\"\\n\\n\"+newState+\"\\n\"+removed);\ntext(\"Rewrote runtime binding, availability comparison, and failed-attempt history rules.\");\n",
