guidance is visible throughout [`system-prompt.md#L102-L147`](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/f97fa5c95010b62ac34c7357f9a1cae6975e12d6/packages/coding-agent/src/prompts/system/system-prompt.md#L102-L147). There is no nested `tools.<tool>` object and no distinction there between registered, active, and bridge-reachable beyond how `toolNames` is assembled.\n\n- System prompt rendering gets one shared context object containing tool names, tool refs, metadata, model/settings flags, skills, rules, workspace, and capability booleans: [`system-prompt.ts#L987-L1033`](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/f97fa5c95010b62ac34c7357f9a1cae6975e12d6/packages/coding-agent/src/system-prompt.ts#L987-L1033). Custom `SYSTEM.md` is loaded through the system-prompt capability and project level wins over user level: [`system-prompt.ts#L487-L505`](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/f97fa5c95010b62ac34c7357f9a1cae6975e12d6/packages/coding-agent/src/system-prompt.ts#L487-L505). It is rendered through `custom-system-prompt.md`: [`custom-system-prompt.md#L1-L64`](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/f97fa5c95010b62ac34c7357f9a1cae6975e12d6/packages/coding-agent/src/prompts/system/custom-system-prompt.md#L1-L64). That customization replaces the system-prompt block; it does not replace built-in tool description files.\n\n- Rebuild timing matters. Tool activation updates the predicate before rebuilding the system prompt, and the rebuild reads current tool descriptions: [`session-tools.ts#L982-L1028`](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/f97fa5c95010b62ac34c7357f9a1cae6975e12d6/packages/coding-agent/src/session/session-tools.ts#L982-L1028). The signature includes current labels, descriptions, and wire names: [`session-tools.ts#L1544-L1577`](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/f97fa5c95010b62ac34c7357f9a1cae6975e12d6/packages/coding-agent/src/session/session-tools.ts#L1544-L1577), [`session-tools.ts#L1584-L1620`](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/f97fa5c95010b62ac34c7357f9a1cae6975e12d6/packages/coding-agent/src/session/session-tools.ts#L1584-L1620). A dynamic getter therefore matters only when a prompt/tool surface rebuild occurs. There are explicit refresh paths, including [`session-tools.ts#L1468-L1501`](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/f97fa5c95010b62ac34c7357f9a1cae6975e12d6/packages/coding-agent/src/session/session-tools.ts#L1468-L1501).\n\nFor llame, the main mismatch is that OMP’s “file-based tool prompts” mean source-controlled Markdown templates, not user-overridable runtime files. Reusing the format and renderer is straightforward; matching customization requires a separate tool-prompt loader/precedence contract and a shared availability context passed to both system and tool description renders.",
